
Directional Substrate Noise Analysis

Exploring how substrate noise spreads across a chip, couples into sensitive circuits, and changes with frequency.
Research Idea
Combine physical modeling with sparse sensing to estimate noise distribution and identify dominant coupling paths. Directionality will be investigated as a consequence of layout, substrate structure, grounding, and source locations.

Key Questions

- Which paths carry the strongest noise toward sensitive blocks?
- How do frequency and grounding change these paths?
- Can a limited number of sensors reconstruct a useful noise map?
- Which placement and isolation changes reduce coupling most effectively?

Planned Approach
Develop substrate network models, simulate noise injection, reconstruct spatial noise maps, and compare predictions against reference simulations.

Intended Outcome
Practical guidance for placement, grounding, and isolation in analog, RF, and mixed-signal ICs.

Status
Early research concept. Modeling and validation are planned.
